<gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="open-pilgrimages" version="1.1"><metadata><name>Sanuki (Temples 65-88, and the return to Temple 1)</name><desc>The last of the four dōjō, and the one that closes the circuit: Temple 65 Sankaku-ji to Temple 88 Ōkubo-ji, then on to Temple 1 Ryōzen-ji where the pilgrimage began — 202.2 km along 24 temple-to-temple henro trail relations. The temples stand closest together here — Temple 68 to Temple 69 is 0.11 km and Temple 72 to Temple 73 is 0.46 km. The last relation is the 39.8 km return from Ōkubo-ji to Ryōzen-ji, and it is the only leg in this section longer than 30 km. Sanuki carries the fourth of the four stages of spiritual progression the pilgrimage maps onto Shikoku&apos;s four provinces: nirvana.</desc><copyright author="OpenStreetMap contributors"><license>https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/</license></copyright><link href="https://open.pilgrimag.es/shikoku-88-sanuki"><text>Sanuki (Temples 65-88, and the return to Temple 1)</text></link></metadata><trk><name>Sanuki (Temples 65-88, and the return to Temple 1)</name><trkseg><trkpt lat="33.967385" lon="133.586898"/><trkpt lat="33.967387" lon="133.586768"/><trkpt lat="33.967383" lon="133.586968"/><trkpt lat="33.967385" lon="133.586898"/><trkpt lat="33.967380" lon="133.587014"/><trkpt lat="33.967383" lon="133.586968"/><trkpt lat="33.967356" lon="133.587289"/><trkpt lat="33.967380" lon="133.587014"/><trkpt lat="33.967332" lon="133.587553"/><trkpt lat="33.967356" lon="133.587289"/><trkpt lat="33.969023" lon="133.592049"/><trkpt lat="33.968902" lon="133.592021"/><trkpt lat="33.968775" lon="133.592044"/><trkpt lat="33.968608" lon="133.592168"/><trkpt lat="33.968497" lon="133.592305"/><trkpt lat="33.968395" lon="133.592388"/><trkpt lat="33.968287" lon="133.592397"/><trkpt lat="33.968150" lon="133.592374"/><trkpt lat="33.967982" lon="133.592314"/><trkpt lat="33.967865" lon="133.592301"/><trkpt lat="33.967732" lon="133.592342"/><trkpt lat="33.967625" lon=